WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.269
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:09.582
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:15.495
Unit nine: Weekend Routines. Today you will describe your weekend with usually and sometimes.

4
00:00:15.795 --> 00:00:18.494
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.701
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.621
Unwind.

7
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:28.278
Unwind means to relax after working hard.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:31.173
I unwind by listening to music.

9
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.320
Your turn. Say: Unwind.

10
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.098
Unwind.

11
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.863
Sleep in.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.813
Sleep in means to sleep later than usual in the morning.

13
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.672
On Sundays, I usually sleep in.

14
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:50.075
Your turn. Say: Sleep in.

15
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:53.888
Sleep in.

16
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.512
Errand.

17
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:59.387
Errand means a short trip to buy or do something.

18
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:01.902
I run errands for my mother.

19
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:04.786
Your turn. Say: Errand.

20
00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:08.414
Errand.

21
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.174
Leisurely.

22
00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:13.322
Leisurely means slow and relaxed.

23
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:15.800
We had a leisurely breakfast.

24
00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:18.941
Your turn. Say: Leisurely.

25
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.022
Leisurely.

26
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.249
Spontaneous.

27
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.575
Spontaneous means done without planning.

28
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.682
We took a spontaneous trip to the river.

29
00:01:32.283 --> 00:01:34.970
Your turn. Say: Spontaneous.

30
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:39.148
Spontaneous.

31
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:40.884
Recharge.

32
00:01:41.883 --> 00:01:44.324
Recharge means to get your energy back.

33
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.672
I need the weekend to recharge.

34
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:49.703
Your turn. Say: Recharge.

35
00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.614
Recharge.

36
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.061
Chore.

37
00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.864
Chore means a small job at home.

38
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.984
Washing dishes is my least favorite chore.

39
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:03.667
Your turn. Say: Chore.

40
00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:07.349
Chore.

41
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.073
Plan ahead.

42
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:12.942
Plan ahead means to plan before something happens.

43
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.084
I plan ahead so I can finish my homework.

44
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:19.487
Your turn. Say: Plan ahead.

45
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:23.555
Plan ahead.

46
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:25.318
Downtime.

47
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:29.187
Downtime means time when you rest and do nothing important.

48
00:02:29.783 --> 00:02:31.527
Everyone needs some downtime.

49
00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:34.456
Your turn. Say: Downtime.

50
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.336
Downtime.

51
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:40.201
Get-together.

52
00:02:41.217 --> 00:02:43.971
Get-together means a small, friendly meeting or party.

53
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:46.943
We have a family get-together on Sunday.

54
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.168
Your turn. Say: Get-together.

55
00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:54.069
Get-together.

56
00:02:54.817 --> 00:02:55.992
Relaxation.

57
00:02:56.983 --> 00:03:00.318
Relaxation means the state of resting and feeling calm.

58
00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:03.613
Reading is my favorite form of relaxation.

59
00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.461
Your turn. Say: Relaxation.

60
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.626
Relaxation.

61
00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:13.431
Refresh.

62
00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:16.881
Refresh means to make you feel less tired.

63
00:03:17.483 --> 00:03:19.657
A swim always refreshes me.

64
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.076
Your turn. Say: Refresh.

65
00:03:25.933 --> 00:03:26.958
Refresh.

66
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:31.592
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.809
Visal, what do you usually do at the weekend?

68
00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:39.739
On Saturday, I usually sleep in and unwind.

69
00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.269
Do you do any chores?

70
00:03:43.383 --> 00:03:47.902
Yes, I sometimes run errands for my mum, like going to the market.

71
00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:50.238
And on Sunday?

72
00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.326
We usually have a family get-together. It helps me recharge for the week.

73
00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:58.130
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:03.177
Grammar focus: usually and sometimes plus present simple.

75
00:04:03.477 --> 00:04:04.710
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:05.417 --> 00:04:06.871
I usually sleep in.

77
00:04:07.783 --> 00:04:09.760
I sometimes run errands.

78
00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.499
She usually visits her grandmother.

79
00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:18.115
Frequency adverbs go before the main verb, but after 'be': I am usually tired.

80
00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:22.629
Be careful! Don't say: I sleep usually in on Sunday.

81
00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:27.182
Say: I usually sleep in on Sunday.

82
00:04:27.482 --> 00:04:29.365
Put 'usually' before the main verb.

83
00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.761
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.044
My Ideal Weekend.

85
00:04:35.344 --> 00:04:37.924
On weekends, I like to sleep in and unwind.

86
00:04:38.933 --> 00:04:41.757
I usually have a leisurely breakfast with my family.

87
00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:46.543
Sometimes I run errands, and I always finish my chores.

88
00:04:47.533 --> 00:04:50.810
In the afternoon, I enjoy some downtime and relaxation.

89
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:55.796
On Sunday evening, we usually have a get-together, and I feel refreshed.

90
00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.867
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:01.717 --> 00:05:03.786
I blank sleep in on Sundays.

92
00:05:04.086 --> 00:05:07.495
A, usually. B, am usually. C, usual.

93
00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:13.044
The answer is A: usually.

94
00:05:14.183 --> 00:05:16.206
A small job at home is a blank.

95
00:05:16.506 --> 00:05:19.800
A, chore. B, errand. C, downtime.

96
00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.217
The answer is A: chore.

97
00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:28.244
Done without planning is blank.

98
00:05:28.544 --> 00:05:33.056
A, spontaneous. B, leisurely. C, relaxing.

99
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.029
The answer is A: spontaneous.

100
00:05:40.233 --> 00:05:43.443
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:44.283 --> 00:05:46.178
Describe your ideal weekend routine.

102
00:05:54.983 --> 00:05:57.227
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:57.527 --> 00:06:07.366
On my ideal weekend, I usually sleep in until eight. Then I sometimes play football, and in the evening I unwind with my family.

104
00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:09.514
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:10.417 --> 00:06:15.879
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and usually and sometimes plus present simple.

106
00:06:16.179 --> 00:06:20.630
Today's value is balance. Enjoy screens a little, then play and read too.

107
00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:23.351
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

108
00:06:23.651 --> 00:06:26.326
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

